test(backend): match Strapi semantics for unset coverages on a draft

Refs: US-02-AC-09, US-02-R1-F01

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


diff --git a/backend/tests/plan-rules.test.ts b/backend/tests/plan-rules.test.ts
index 2fda85c..cd05a8e 100644
--- a/backend/tests/plan-rules.test.ts
+++ b/backend/tests/plan-rules.test.ts
@@ -247,10 +247,11 @@ describe('US-02-BR-01 ADR-0001 plan rules (key per country, required country, at
       expect(await plans.findOne({ documentId: draft, status: 'published' })).toBeNull();
     }, 60_000);

-    it('US-02-AC-09 refuses to publish an existing draft whose coverages were never set', async () => {
-      const draft = await createPlan('probe-draft-unset-publish', colombia, 'draft', { coverages: undefined });
-      await expect(plans.publish({ documentId: draft })).rejects.toThrow();
-      expect(await plans.findOne({ documentId: draft, status: 'published' })).toBeNull();
+    // Strapi semantics (required + min 1 on a repeatable component): an unset list is refused even on a draft,
+    // while a draft may hold [] (the admin panel and REST send [] for an empty repeatable) and then cannot be published.
+    it('US-02-AC-09 refuses to create a draft with coverages unset (no draft without a list); the draft with [] is covered above', async () => {
+      await expect(createPlan('probe-draft-unset', colombia, 'draft', { coverages: undefined })).rejects.toThrow();
+      expect(await plans.findMany({ status: 'draft', filters: { key: 'probe-draft-unset' } })).toEqual([]);
     }, 60_000);

     it('US-02-AC-09 refuses to publish a draft whose coverages an editor emptied after saving it valid', async () => {
23:  `strictRelations`, typed attributes instead of free JSON, draft vs active).
44:- A `plan` content type in Strapi with a required `country` relation, draft & publish, the
47:  including one draft-only and one inactive plan per country.
106:| US-02-BR-02 | Story: "Only published and active plans for the country are shown." | A plan is shown on step 2 of country C if and only if its published version exists, that published version has `isActive = true`, it is related to C, and it is well-formed (BR-01). Draft-only plans, published plans with `isActive = false`, plans of other countries and malformed plans are never shown. When a published plan also has unpublished draft changes, the **published** version is shown (US-02-Q-10). Offered plans are shown in `sortOrder` ascending; ties are broken by `key` ascending (US-02-Q-11). The recommended plan keeps its configured position. With zero offered plans, step 2 shows the "no plans available" state (US-02-Q-15). | US-02-AC-01, US-02-AC-04, US-02-AC-08 |
110:| US-02-BR-06 | Assessment: "Changing a form field or a plan in Strapi must be reflected in the app without changing code."; "form and plans 100% configurable from Strapi". | Publishing, unpublishing, activating, deactivating or editing a plan (name, description, price, coverages, benefits, order, recommended flag) is reflected on step 2 on the next full page load, with no code change, build or deployment; no browser or proxy cache delays it (US-01-Q-16, ADR-0002). No plan name, price, coverage or benefit exists in front-end code. Unpublished drafts are never readable by an anonymous caller, also with `status=draft` (ADR-0002). | US-02-AC-08, US-02-AC-12, US-02-AC-14, US-02-AC-19 |
144:    | Colombia | "Plan Básico", "Plan Clásico", "Plan Total"         | "Plan Joven" (draft only), "Plan Total Plus" (inactive), any Chile plan |
145:    | Chile    | "Plan Esencial", "Plan Protegido", "Plan Premium"   | "Plan Flex" (draft only), "Plan Premium Plus" (inactive), any Colombia plan |
286:    | draft only     | true   | Colombia | not shown |
291:  And an editor saved, without publishing, a draft of it with base price 1600000
421:    | valid step 1 data and the chosen plan "joven" (draft only) | /co/planes |
491:Scenario Outline: Anonymous requests never return draft plans
493:    with "status=draft" and "filters[key][$eq]=joven" through <entry point>
511:The draft rows are fewer than US-01-AC-28 because the published-only middleware is shared and
533:| US-02-Q-10 | Active vs published: what is `isActive` for if drafts exist? Default value? What if a published plan has newer unpublished changes? Can anonymous callers read inactive plans? | Editors need to know which switch hides a plan; the request filter and the boundary must agree. | Publishing makes a plan available; `isActive = false` hides a published plan without unpublishing it (for example a paused offer). `isActive` defaults to `true`. The published version is shown even when a newer draft exists (AC-08). Inactive published plans are readable through the public API by a caller who omits the filter; accepted, as they are not secret (unreleased plans stay drafts). The front end requests `isActive = true` and also drops any inactive plan at the boundary. | Default accepted. — Felipe Sabogal, 2026-11-21 (HC1) |
555:### 7.1 `plan` collection type (per country, draft & publish on)
620:| CO (COP, es-CO) | `basico` → Plan Básico 850000; `clasico` → Plan Clásico 1400000; `total` → Plan Total 2100000 | `clasico` | `joven` → Plan Joven (draft only, sortOrder 25); `total-plus` → Plan Total Plus (published, `isActive` false) |
621:| CL (CLP, es-CL) | `esencial` → Plan Esencial 290000; `protegido` → Plan Protegido 480000; `premium` → Plan Premium 720000 | `protegido` | `flex` → Plan Flex (draft only, sortOrder 15); `premium-plus` → Plan Premium Plus (published, `isActive` false) |
715:  justified in §7.5; reads through the GET-only proxy; drafts never anonymous (AC-19). The price
765:| `plans-cl-content` | US-02-AC-01 (CL), AC-02, AC-06 (CL rendering), AC-07 (CL), AC-08 (seeded rows), AC-12, AC-19 (draft and write scenarios, Node process, no browser) |
778:| US-02-AC-08 | unit (parser drops inactive) + e2e (seeded draft-only and inactive plans) + manual (published version with a pending draft, in the Strapi admin at HC3) | `plan.spec.ts`, `plans-cl-content`; HC3 check |
803:| 2026-11-21 | spec-writer (Claude Opus 5.5) | 1 Spec | Draft v0.1 | First version from story.md, the Assessment requirements, US-01 spec v0.5 and ADR-0001..0006. 7 BR, 19 AC (4 original, 15 derived), 20 gaps (4 block HC1: Q-01 price rule [ADR], Q-02 plan currency, Q-03 summary route, Q-04 e2e files), 1 ADR needed plus 1 candidate. Seed annex [seed-plans.md](seed-plans.md). |

